                <pb facs="0559" n="453" xml:id="pg453"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Barrett to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1906-04-19"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">April 19, 1906</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 73.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Replying to your No. 16 of March 19 in
                    regard to the additional duty of 8 cents imposed on foreign flour, in which you
                    say, “It would appear that the figures given by you state the duty in Colombian
                    currency. If so, the equivalent in American gold might be stated for greater
                    convenience,” I have the honor to observe that this 8 cents is gold valuation
                    and not what might be termed ordinary Colombian currency. In fact all customs
                    duties in Colombia are stated practically in gold.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Barrett.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
